    "evidence": "Employee 4471's timesheet for the week commencing 19 October 2026 does not support 42 hours. Breaks are unpaid and deducted from time on site, so paid hours are: Mon 08:00-16:30 = 8.50h less 30m = 8.00h; Tue 08:00-17:00 = 9.00h less 45m = 8.25h; Wed 07:30-16:00 = 8.50h less 30m = 8.00h; Thu 08:00-16:15 = 8.25h less 30m = 7.75h; Fri 08:00-17:00 = 9.00h less 30m = 8.50h. Total paid time = 40.50 hours, not 42. Even on the most generous reading, gross time on site before any breaks is 8.50 + 9.00 + 8.50 + 8.25 + 9.00 = 43.25 hours, which is also not 42. Reaching 42.00 would require deducting only 75 minutes of the 165 minutes of recorded unpaid breaks, i.e. ignoring breaks on two of the five days. Saturday 24 and Sunday 25 October have no clock times recorded, and no overtime was approved this week, so nothing further can be added. Uncertainty: the timesheet is the only evidence in the case and the clock times are taken as printed from the door terminal with no manual corrections.",
